  "notes": [
    "cache_write_per_million is the provider's 30-minute cache-write price and cache_write_1h_per_million its 12-hour price: the ledger reads the second key as 'the dearest write', whatever its retention.",
    "cache_writes_unreported: the pricing page lists write prices without saying which usage field reports written tokens, so every uncached token Entroly is charged for is priced as a 12-hour write.",
    "priced_up_to_input_tokens: the page has a Short/Long context switch but states no threshold. Requests above 200,000 input tokens (below the 272,000-token threshold OpenAI states for GPT-5.5) get no price.",
    "Only models whose price was read from the linked OpenAI page on verified_at are listed. Anything else has no bundled price; use ENTROLY_PRICING_CATALOG."
